{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794522948633,"sessionID":"ses_e2e198e88ffeLY7qjYK4q8qPph","part":{"partID":"prt_1d1e722a00010KTbOavvhg673h","sessionID":"ses_e2e198e88ffeLY7qjYK4q8qPph","messageID":"msg_1d1e6fef1001fWBhc7eXmbT8je","type":"tool","id":"call_0e17d06832b3464096d16586","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"measure-embedder-cost|cold\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md | head -30"},"output":"58:- **Measurement script** (`ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`): without it the cost in the install guides is a one-off reading nobody can reproduce, which is what the brief's first reading is today.\n87:Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n95:Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n105:| Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n109:| Manual | The script on the build machine, once warm and once after the 5 minute unload | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` |\n147:| Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"58:- **Measurement script** (`ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs`): without it the cost in the install guides is a one-off reading nobody can reproduce, which is what the brief's first reading is today.\n87:Matrix axes for the degrade test: server reachable or absent, model pulled or missing, answer inside or past the deadline, model warm or cold. The test holds one row per failure value plus a warm row and a cold-inside-deadline row, six rows in total.\n95:Setup records the before numbers, the hook timing and the cold-load behaviour after an aborted call. Implementation adds the script, the deadline, the status fields, the warning, the route, the setup leg and the guide text in the waves `tasks.md` lists. Verification reruns the script, both captures, the floor, the rollup, the hook timing and both test suites. The ordered work and each task's check are in `tasks.md`.\n105:| Unit | The prompt embedding with an injected adapter: warm, cold inside the deadline, absent, model missing, past the deadline and the warning | Vitest, `tests/semantic-prompt-embedding-degrade.vitest.ts` with `VITEST` stubbed off inside the test |\n109:| Manual | The script on the build machine, once warm and once after the 5 minute unload | `node ADV/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` |\n147:| Implementation | The before numbers and the cold-load reading | Verification |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"rg -n \\\"measure-embedder-cost|cold\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/008-embedder-setup-and-cost/plan.md | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794522948256,"end":1794522948633}}}}
